  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1afd3f0ae2ece544a87007c165ec87d0, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogue:
    sentences:
    - '???: I need your help! '
    - Your eyes slowly focus on what appears to be a... fairy?
    - '???: I''m not a fairy! I''m far more powerful than Tooth or Bel - I''ll have
      you know. '
    - 'You: Who are you?'
    - 'Not-Fairy: Just call me Yota for now. I need you to get up right now.'
    - 'You: It''s a Saturday. I usually sleep in - you know?'
    - 'Yota: You''re a rat, for Toys'' sake! You have no concept of a weekend.'
    - 'You: Fair point. What do you want, o powerful Not-Fairy?'
    - 'Yota: You know who''s room you''re living in - don''t you? I know rats aren''t
      the brightest... or the cleanest or the nicest or the - '
    - 'You: What''s your point?'
    - 'Yota: Right, sorry. Stupid mouth, stupid mouth.'
    - 'You: I thought I wasn''t the brightest.'
    - 'Yota: I never said I was either but that''s beside''s the point! Stop distracting
      me! I need your help with fixing something.'
    - 'You: I don''t know if you remember but I''m not the brightest and I''m not
      exactly the most dextrous either.'
    - Yota:That's why I'm here! The little girl who's room you're living in - remember
      her? Well her toy world is disappearing. That poor girl must be going through
      something that's destroying her imagination.
    - 'You: Toy world? Uh-huh.'
    - 'Yota: Don''t you sneak in here and look at her stuff? How do you live in her
      room and not know what toys are?'
    - 'You: I''m-'
    - 'Yota: Right, right, not the brightest. Never mind. Point is you have to help
      me - only you can. '
    - 'You: Why me?'
    - 'Yota: Because! When the toy world disappears it fractures and leaks into the
      real world until nothing is left. The others are from the toy world - they
      can''t touch anything in this world and well, I''m not exactly dextrous either,
      so enter Rat...'
    - 'You: Hmm. I get it. So, I''m the chosen hero that the whole of the toy world
      depends on?'
    - 'Yota: Yes! Exactly! Well, not exactly - just this little girl''s toy world,
      not the whole of the toy world. They have me for that, hehe.'
    - 'You: Well, that''s wonderful except I''m no hero, dust mite. What''s in it
      for me?'
    - 'Dust Mite?: I''ll pretend I didn''t hear the "dust mite." '
    - 'You: Just answer the question.'
    - 'Not-Dust-Mite-Just-Yota: You''ve never wanted to go out there? Look at this
      place - you barely have any room to breathe let alone live! You don''t have
      any friends or family and I can bet a wing and ring that you''re afraid of
      her. When was the last you looked at anything else other than these three corners
      and a block of cheese?'
    - 'You: I''ll pretend i didn''t hear the "cheese'' stereotype. That''s for mice
      by the way.'
    - 'Yota: Someone is avoiding the question, hehe.'
    - 'You: All right. All right. You might not be so bright, Yota but you''ve got
      keen observation skills. I''ll help you'
    - 'Yota: Yes! Thank you! If you weren''t a disease infested rodent and I wasn''t
      a holy celestial being I''d kiss you!'
    - 'You: Sure, thanks. Let''s just go before i change my mind.'
    - 'Yota: Here''s what you have to do. Her toy Jenni figurine: her toy spirit 
      has already fractured into 5 pieces and leaked into the real world. You have
      to find all of her and bring her back to where her toy spirit was born'
    - 'You: Where her toy spirirt was born?'
    - 'Yota: I don''t know what it''s called in the real world but it''s where she
      stopped being just a toy and became part of a child''s imagination. Without
      that imagination there would be no toy world. Think of it as the place where
      Jenni first came out of so that our little girl and play with her for the first
      time.'
    - 'Yota: Once you''ve done that you need to help the mechanic. He''s fractured
      too but luckily he''s still in the toy world so you wont be able to talk to
      touch him unless you''re a toy. I''ll use my powers to help you Imbue her'
    - 'Rat: So, what you''re gonna use your Not-Fairy magic and turn me into a toy?'
    - 'Yota: You''re sarcastic but you''re not far off-

      You: What?'
    - 'Yota: Once you return Jenni''s spirit to her place of birth I''ll use my magic
      to help you "imbue" her. Your true form will remain untouched and you''ll likely
      want to go back to it when you need to make contact with anything in the real
      world. Just go back to the birth place when you need to change.'
    - 'Yota: Remember, rats cannot interact with the toy world; everything will just
      look like an inamnimate object to you. As Jenni you also won''t be able to
      venture out of the barrier I set up to protect what''s left of the world. '
    - 'You: Collect Right. It''s now or never while she''s outside. Come on. '
    - And so your journey begins...
